From ed887723535514b0b8d18474227a2464627717ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: frapercan <frapercan1@alum.us.es>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:47:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Count discarded tasks and crashed workers; optionally
 fail the run

A task that failed in a worker was logged and dropped, a worker process
that crashed (e.g. OOM-killed) went unnoticed, and start() returned
normally either way. Callers could not tell that results were missing:
FANTASIA lost a whole lookup batch to an alignment error and still exited
with 0.

Count, in a multiprocessing.Value shared with the worker processes:
- inserting-queue failures, and computing-queue failures after the retry;
- worker processes that exit with a non-zero code.
At the end of start(), after post-processing so partial results are still
written, log the count as an error. With the new option
fail_on_task_errors: True, raise TaskFailuresError instead. The default is
False so that existing pipelines (e.g. `pis`, whose stages run in sequence)
keep running past a bad record; FANTASIA opts in.

ValueError from process() remains a "skip" for backward compatibility, but
skipped tasks are now counted and reported. Counters are reset on every
start(), and the failure count is logged even when post-processing fails.
